11.2 A recovery round (bounded by roundBudgetMs and maxAttemptsPerRound):
1. Identify and classify the failure (10).
2. Decide whether it is transient: one quick retry on the same path after a short delay.
3. Check whether the network changed; if so, reassess it first (12).
4. Reassess the underlay (7). If international connectivity is broadly down, do not rotate servers; go to step 7.
5. Test whether the current server is reachable (9.2).
6. Evaluate alternatives in order: other user-supplied profiles of the same gateway (different port, transport or relay), then other user-configured servers by score, then runtime variants if enabled (13).
7. Evaluate authorized relays if configured (14).
8. Select a viable path, connect and verify real tunnel traffic (9.4). If verification fails, roll back to the previous best path or continue the round.
9. Record the result; update scores and breakers; skip known-failed paths.
10. If nothing is viable, enter LONG_OUTAGE_WAIT and report the real limitation.
