11.4 Selection and user intent.
• A user-pinned server is never replaced automatically unless allowAutoServerSwitch is ON; retries and variants of the pinned server are allowed.
• UNTRUSTED paths (AutoVpnDiscoveryEngine) are used for automatic recovery only in Free VPN mode (if present) or when the user explicitly enabled auto-discovery. They are scored with the trust factor, never outrank user-owned profiles, and their probing stays within the existing discovery budgets.
• SmartFailoverManager keeps ownership of «which profile next». The engine adds evidence gating, path candidates, backoff, breakers and verification.
11.5 Backoff, circuit breaker, long outage.
• Exponential backoff with jitter: base 2 s, factor 2, jitter ±20%, cap 5 min; reset after a verified connection that stays up through the stability window.
• Per-path circuit breaker: opens after 3 consecutive failures for 5 min, doubling up to a 60 min cap; half-open allows one trial. Failures caused by network conditions (timeouts, resets, DNS) drop to half-open when the transport kind changes.
• Round limits: at most 5 candidates, 6 attempts and 60 s per round.
• Long-outage polling ladder: 30 s, 60 s, 2 min, 5 min, 10 min, then 15 min as the cap; immediate reassessment on a network event or user action; automatic resume when connectivity returns.
11.6 No-leak invariants.
• Prefer restarting only the Xray core or its outbounds and keeping the TUN descriptor open, so no packet leaves outside the tunnel during recovery. While the core is down, packets routed into the TUN are dropped, which acts as a kill switch, provided the TUN routes capture all traffic (verify in the audit).
• If TUN parameters must change, prefer establishing the replacement interface before closing the old descriptor, verify the behavior on a device, and never leave two active TUNs.
• Do not use allowBypass or per-app bypass as part of recovery.
• Respect the existing kill-switch settings.
11.7 Anti-loop guarantees. A global cap on engine-initiated restarts per window (default 6 per 10 min), after which the engine goes to LONG_OUTAGE_WAIT; a restart-storm guard persisted in DataStore with timestamps so repeated service restarts cannot loop; no recovery action may trigger another assessment without passing the debounce and rate limits.
11.8 Integration. Define a narrow interface (for example ConnectivityAdvisor) consumed by SmartFailoverManager: given the latest failure and assessment it returns advice (retry, switch, wait, stop) with reason codes. SmartFailoverManager remains the executor of profile switching unless the audit shows a cleaner seam. If the engine throws or a flag disables it, the VPN keeps working in legacy mode (fail open to the old behavior; log a sanitized message).
12. Multi-network support and network switching
12.1 NetworkMonitor. A callbackFlow over registerNetworkCallback with a request for physical networks (NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET and NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VPN), plus the default-network callback if the audit finds it useful. Track the set of available networks and their capabilities. Emit conflated, debounced events (default debounce 800 ms). Unregister in awaitClose and on service stop. Do not use deprecated polling APIs (getActiveNetworkInfo, getAllNetworks, NetworkInfo).
